 echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186558929 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186124477 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124290 #edb/ref 1759